<item><title>Sierra Leone charcoal trade sustains families as tree loss threatens land</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-families-as-tree-loss-a237a3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-families-as-tree-loss-a237a3/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A government energy compact says only 15% of the population has access to clean cooking, while charcoal production removes trees.</description><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:58:18 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone regulator reports NLE 7.4 million in 2024 revenue</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>The Sierra Leone Electricity and Water Regulatory Commission said levies and licences brought in the income, up from NLE 2.3 million in 2023.</description><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:58:18 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/share.jpg" length="41494" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
